WEBVTT


00:00:00.520 --> 00:00:03.520
Or sit here and make up the words


00:00:03.600 --> 00:00:06.600
As we go along


00:00:07.920 --> 00:00:10.759
They told me maybe she's crazy


00:00:10.760 --> 00:00:13.159
A little like you


00:00:13.160 --> 00:00:16.160
Everyone said you were nothing but trouble


00:00:17.000 --> 00:00:20.000
And all that I know
is that I've never been here before


00:00:23.040 --> 00:00:26.040
I don't need to pretend anymore


00:00:33.920 --> 00:00:36.479
Strange, so strange


00:00:36.480 --> 00:00:37.759
You are hilarious.


00:00:37.760 --> 00:00:40.760
When it feels better being alone


00:00:41.760 --> 00:00:44.760
You'll accept there is nobody else


00:00:45.360 --> 00:00:47.599
Then set it in stone


00:00:49.680 --> 00:00:52.679
And they told me maybe she's crazy


00:00:52.680 --> 00:00:54.439
A little like you


00:00:55.440 --> 00:00:58.440
Everyone said...


00:01:02.720 --> 00:01:05.720
Will and I were just updating our band's
MySpace page.


00:01:14.800 --> 00:01:17.800
You know that kid, Will Burton?
Do some recon.


00:01:18.080 --> 00:01:19.119
Find out everything you can about him.


00:01:19.120 --> 00:01:22.120
They'll have his records in the office.
Where he's from, where he went to school.


00:01:22.360 --> 00:01:25.319
His guidance counsellor report,
that'll have all the good stuff. All right?


00:01:25.320 --> 00:01:26.919
Everything. And do it today.


00:01:26.920 --> 00:01:29.759
Whoa. Yo, dude,
we don't actually work for you.


00:01:29.760 --> 00:01:32.760
It's not like you're the Joker
and we're your henchmen.


00:01:35.000 --> 00:01:38.000
Fine. I'll do it myself.


00:01:38.480 --> 00:01:41.480
All right, best for last. Sa5m, Will?
Tell us who you are.


00:01:51.560 --> 00:01:54.560
My project is Will Burton.


00:01:55.640 --> 00:01:58.640
I'm pointing
because it's hard to tell who he is.


00:02:00.520 --> 00:02:03.520
I was going to use photographs
for this presentation,


00:02:04.040 --> 00:02:07.040
but then I realized, the real Will Burton
can't be captured on film.


00:02:10.440 --> 00:02:13.279
Instead,


00:02:13.280 --> 00:02:15.919
you need this.


00:02:15.920 --> 00:02:18.920
Will is a reflective surface.


00:02:19.320 --> 00:02:22.320
He mirrors back at you
whatever you want to see.


00:02:23.680 --> 00:02:26.680
He reflects you back to you.


00:02:26.760 --> 00:02:29.760
And it's nice for awhile.


00:02:29.920 --> 00:02:32.679
You stop feeling lonely.


00:02:32.680 --> 00:02:35.680
But then you realize,
he's doing that with everyone.


00:02:39.520 --> 00:02:42.520
The only person he can't do it for


00:02:43.400 --> 00:02:45.039
is Will.


00:02:45.040 --> 00:02:48.040
Because he doesn't have a clue


00:02:48.120 --> 00:02:51.120
who he is.


00:03:00.760 --> 00:03:03.679
Okay, well, that was very creative.


00:03:03.680 --> 00:03:06.680
And really mean. Okay, Will, you're up.


00:04:01.800 --> 00:04:04.800
If I told you things I did before


00:04:05.160 --> 00:04:08.160
Told you how I used to be


00:04:08.440 --> 00:04:11.440
Would you go along with someone like me?


00:04:14.920 --> 00:04:17.920
If you knew my story word for word


00:04:18.560 --> 00:04:21.560
Had all of my history


00:04:21.840 --> 00:04:24.840
Would you go along with someone like me?


00:04:27.280 --> 00:04:30.280
And we don't care about the young folks


00:04:31.000 --> 00:04:33.879
Talking about the young style


00:04:33.880 --> 00:04:36.879
And we don't care about the old folks


00:04:36.880 --> 00:04:39.880
Talking about the old style too


00:04:40.560 --> 00:04:43.560
And we don't care about our own faults


00:04:44.320 --> 00:04:47.239
Talking about our own style


00:04:47.240 --> 00:04:49.919
All we care about is talking


00:04:49.920 --> 00:04:52.920
Talking only me and you


00:04:53.920 --> 00:04:56.920
And we don't care about the young folks


00:04:57.600 --> 00:05:00.599
Talking about the young style


00:05:00.600 --> 00:05:03.479
And we don't care about the old folks


00:05:03.480 --> 00:05:06.480
Talking about the old style too


00:05:07.240 --> 00:05:10.240
And we don't care about our own faults


00:05:10.760 --> 00:05:13.719
Talking about our own style


00:05:13.720 --> 00:05:16.720
All we care about is talking


00:05:16.800 --> 00:05:19.800
Talking only me and you


00:05:20.160 --> 00:05:22.519
Talking only me and you


00:05:30.320 --> 00:05:31.919
Dear David Bowie,


00:05:31.920 --> 00:05:34.920
sometimes it seems like things
actually work out.


00:05:40.840 --> 00:05:43.840
English, Irene. English. There is
no such thing as conversational Elvish.


00:05:47.560 --> 00:05:50.560
Sorry, Dewey.


00:05:52.360 --> 00:05:54.639
It's what they call you, isn't it?


00:05:54.640 --> 00:05:55.959
No.


00:05:55.960 --> 00:05:58.960
It was at your last school.
Or do you prefer "Junior"?


00:05:59.000 --> 00:06:01.519
Do you know your buddy,
his full name is Will Burton, Jr.?


00:06:01.520 --> 00:06:02.999
Did you know that I don't care?


00:06:03.000 --> 00:06:04.759
Well, he told you
his dad was famous, right?


00:06:04.760 --> 00:06:07.599
Or infamous, right, Dewey?
I mean, you still close to the old man?


00:06:07.600 --> 00:06:09.319
You probably don't get to talk to him
much anymore, do you?


00:06:09.320 --> 00:06:12.320
-I don't know what you're talking about.
-Well, I think you do, Dewey.


00:06:13.080 --> 00:06:16.080
I think you do, Dewey.


00:06:22.240 --> 00:06:25.240
Okay, that was surreal. Are you okay?


00:06:26.040 --> 00:06:29.040
I don't... I got... I gotta...


00:06:38.840 --> 00:06:40.959
What are you doing?


00:06:40.960 --> 00:06:43.960
You didn't answer my texts,
and you left me alone with the monsters.


00:06:44.400 --> 00:06:46.479
Sorry, I'm sick.


00:06:46.480 --> 00:06:49.480
My spidey-sense tells me you're lying.


00:06:50.880 --> 00:06:53.159
I'm thinking about changing schools.


00:06:53.160 --> 00:06:56.160
No way, my little friend. I'm not facing
the Neanderthals without you.


00:06:56.440 --> 00:06:59.440
Besides, if you change schools,
then you can't gain access to this.


00:07:02.720 --> 00:07:05.239
-What's that?
-Something private.


00:07:05.240 --> 00:07:08.240
Something I would only show
the manager of my band.


00:07:08.800 --> 00:07:11.639
Or my best friend.


00:07:11.640 --> 00:07:14.640
Scooch.


00:07:15.000 --> 00:07:18.000
Okay. You said we needed one song
that says who we are.


00:07:18.360 --> 00:07:21.360
Well, these say who I am.


00:07:23.680 --> 00:07:26.680
Little brothers.


00:07:26.960 --> 00:07:29.960
Little brothers again.


00:07:31.520 --> 00:07:33.519
-For your dad?
-No.


00:07:33.520 --> 00:07:35.999
Not for him, exactly.


00:07:36.000 --> 00:07:38.239
Inspired by him, I guess.
You know, things he said to me.


00:07:38.240 --> 00:07:41.240
But it's not just about my dad anymore.
That'd be, hello, weird.


00:07:41.680 --> 00:07:44.599
It's about everything.


00:07:44.600 --> 00:07:46.839
Wow, that's articulate.


00:07:46.840 --> 00:07:48.119
You know, there's other stuff in here, too.


00:07:48.120 --> 00:07:51.120
-I'm not saying any of it's good...
-Thanks.


00:07:51.480 --> 00:07:54.480
Hey. By accepting this, it means that there
will be no more talk of changing schools.


00:07:57.120 --> 00:08:00.120
Agreed?


00:08:01.040 --> 00:08:03.719
-Man, I'm good.
-Charlotte!


00:08:03.720 --> 00:08:06.319
-Charlotte! My mom is in the...
-I knew you were ticklish.


00:08:06.320 --> 00:08:09.320
You are so ticklish, I knew it.


00:08:10.400 --> 00:08:13.400
Somebody wanna tell me
what's going on in here?


00:08:16.400 --> 00:08:18.359
Get off his bed.


00:08:18.360 --> 00:08:20.479
Wait. You don't think...


00:08:21.520 --> 00:08:23.959
I saw you kiss him in the car.


00:08:23.960 --> 00:08:26.079
Well, that was
for educational purposes only.


00:08:26.080 --> 00:08:27.159
I wanna die.


00:08:27.160 --> 00:08:29.599
Did you hear that? He wants to die.
He needs help, Karen.


00:08:29.600 --> 00:08:31.719
Then I'll help him. I'm his mom.


00:08:31.720 --> 00:08:33.799
But I am wise in the ways of Will.


00:08:33.800 --> 00:08:36.800
I'm actually here, you know. These covers
don't literally make me disappear.


00:08:38.240 --> 00:08:40.719
You know what I think?
I think you're full of it, Charlotte.


00:08:40.720 --> 00:08:43.119
And when I think someone's full of it,
I don't trust them.


00:08:43.120 --> 00:08:45.119
Mom, will you stop interfering?


00:08:45.120 --> 00:08:47.959
Sorry, I'm not your friend,
I'm your mother. That's my job.


00:08:47.960 --> 00:08:50.960
No, Mom, you're supposed to give me
a little breathing room so I can have a life,


00:08:52.240 --> 00:08:54.599
instead of just saying that's what you want.


00:08:54.600 --> 00:08:57.319
-He's got a point, Karen.
-And you, I'm not a manager.


00:08:57.320 --> 00:09:00.320
I don't take on the biggest band
in school and change destiny. I can't.


00:09:02.840 --> 00:09:05.840
Will you both just please leave me alone?


00:09:10.240 --> 00:09:13.240
Get out.


00:09:23.000 --> 00:09:26.000
-Somebody called me Dewey today.
-What? How?


00:09:26.400 --> 00:09:29.400
-He must've found out about Dad.
-I hate them all.


00:09:29.480 --> 00:09:31.759
-Me too.
-You, however, I love.


00:09:31.760 --> 00:09:34.760
Yeah, but you married Dad.
We can't really trust your taste.


00:09:36.040 --> 00:09:39.040
I was 19. And he was a drummer.


00:09:39.720 --> 00:09:42.720
And overnight it made my mother
finally take me seriously,


00:09:43.000 --> 00:09:44.479
which is really all I wanted.


00:09:44.480 --> 00:09:45.559
-Mom?
-I... What?


00:09:45.560 --> 00:09:48.560
You're doing that thing
where you talk to me like I'm Oprah.


00:09:48.640 --> 00:09:51.640
I'll tell you this, though.
I'd marry him all over again to get you.


00:09:57.920 --> 00:10:00.920
I promise you're going to get
everything you deserve out of life.


00:10:01.920 --> 00:10:04.920
And a little bit of the next guy's.


00:10:14.720 --> 00:10:17.519
I'll never be


00:10:17.520 --> 00:10:20.520
A knight in armor with a sword in hand


00:10:22.640 --> 00:10:25.640
Ora kamikaze fighter


00:10:26.640 --> 00:10:29.439
Don't count on me


00:10:29.440 --> 00:10:32.440
To storm the barricades and take a stand


00:10:35.240 --> 00:10:38.240
Or hold my ground


00:10:39.080 --> 00:10:42.080
You'll never see any scars or wounds


00:10:43.880 --> 00:10:46.679
I don't walk on coals


00:10:46.680 --> 00:10:49.680
I won't walk on water


00:10:50.600 --> 00:10:53.439
I am no prince


00:10:53.440 --> 00:10:56.239
I am no saint


00:10:56.240 --> 00:10:59.240
I am not anyone's wildest dream


00:11:01.680 --> 00:11:04.680
But I will stand behind


00:11:05.560 --> 00:11:08.560
And be someone to fall back on


00:11:17.880 --> 00:11:20.880
That's the song.


00:11:29.440 --> 00:11:31.799
Some comedy


00:11:31.800 --> 00:11:33.639
You're bruised and beaten down


00:11:33.640 --> 00:11:36.640
And I am the one who's looking for a favor


00:11:38.680 --> 00:11:41.039
Still, honestly


00:11:41.040 --> 00:11:44.040
You don't believe me
But the things I have


00:11:44.680 --> 00:11:47.680
Are the things you need


00:11:48.120 --> 00:11:51.120
You look at me like I don't make sense


00:11:51.920 --> 00:11:54.920
Like a waste of time
Like it serves no purpose


00:11:57.200 --> 00:12:00.200
I am no prince
I am no saint


00:12:01.880 --> 00:12:04.880
And if that's what you believe you need


00:12:06.560 --> 00:12:09.560
You're wrong
You don't need much


00:12:09.920 --> 00:12:12.920
You need someone to fall back on


00:12:15.680 --> 00:12:18.680
And I'll be that
I'll take your side


00:12:20.200 --> 00:12:23.200
If I'm the only one


00:12:23.520 --> 00:12:26.520
I'm used to that


00:12:27.200 --> 00:12:29.479
I've been alone


00:12:29.480 --> 00:12:32.480
I'd rather be


00:12:34.040 --> 00:12:36.599
The half of us


00:12:36.600 --> 00:12:38.799
The least of you


00:12:38.800 --> 00:12:41.800
The best of me


00:12:43.400 --> 00:12:45.719
And I will be


00:12:45.720 --> 00:12:48.720
I'll be your prince
I'll be your saint


00:12:50.280 --> 00:12:53.280
I will go crashing through fences
in your name


00:12:56.040 --> 00:12:58.319
I will, I swear


00:12:58.320 --> 00:13:01.320
I'll be someone to fall back on


00:13:02.680 --> 00:13:05.680
I'll be the one who waits


00:13:06.360 --> 00:13:09.360
And for as long as you let me


00:13:10.120 --> 00:13:13.120
I will be the one you need


00:13:14.600 --> 00:13:17.600
I'll be someone to fall back on


00:13:31.240 --> 00:13:34.240
Someone to fall back on


00:13:41.720 --> 00:13:44.720
One to fall back on


00:13:55.320 --> 00:13:58.320
Dear David Bowie,


00:13:59.120 --> 00:14:02.120
just when it looked like things
might be okay,


00:14:03.160 --> 00:14:04.479
disaster struck.


00:14:04.480 --> 00:14:07.119
What's going on? Where is everybody?


00:14:07.120 --> 00:14:10.120
-Art class is cancelled today.
-Why? What happened?


00:14:12.280 --> 00:14:15.280
Charlotte's father passed away.


00:14:16.640 --> 00:14:19.479
I assumed you knew.


00:14:19.480 --> 00:14:22.480
No.


00:14:33.920 --> 00:14:36.920
This was a mistake. We shouldn't be here.


00:14:37.440 --> 00:14:40.440
She didn't return any of my calls.


00:14:42.640 --> 00:14:44.839
-You going to be okay?
-Yeah.


00:14:44.840 --> 00:14:47.479
Okay.


00:14:47.480 --> 00:14:50.480
Go, she's your friend. She needs you.


00:14:59.400 --> 00:15:02.400
- Boys...
- I got them.


00:15:11.840 --> 00:15:14.840
Charlotte?


00:15:16.160 --> 00:15:19.160
I'm sorry.


00:15:21.680 --> 00:15:23.119
I called.


00:15:23.120 --> 00:15:26.120
I don't know if you got any of my messages.


00:15:28.040 --> 00:15:31.040
Yeah, I got them. Thanks.


00:15:32.400 --> 00:15:35.399
I wish you would've called me back.


00:15:35.400 --> 00:15:36.839
Why?


00:15:36.840 --> 00:15:38.279
"Why?"


00:15:38.280 --> 00:15:40.919
I don't know. I mean, you told Ben.


00:15:40.920 --> 00:15:43.559
So?


00:15:43.560 --> 00:15:44.679
Is anything wrong?


00:15:44.680 --> 00:15:46.159
Yeah.


00:15:46.160 --> 00:15:47.399
Yeah, my dad died.


00:15:47.400 --> 00:15:48.959
No, I know.


00:15:48.960 --> 00:15:51.960
I wish I could've met him.
I'm sure he was a great man.


00:15:54.760 --> 00:15:57.760
He was.


00:15:58.400 --> 00:16:01.400
I got to do this.


00:16:02.920 --> 00:16:05.239
Charlotte.


00:16:05.240 --> 00:16:08.240
Charlotte.


00:16:08.720 --> 00:16:10.439
-What do you want, Will?
-What do I want?


00:16:10.440 --> 00:16:12.279
I just want you to know that I'm here
for you.


00:16:12.280 --> 00:16:14.039
Okay, got it. What else?


00:16:14.040 --> 00:16:16.959
And not to worry about the daycare.
I can handle that until you come back.


00:16:16.960 --> 00:16:18.039
That's it.


00:16:18.040 --> 00:16:19.039
Listen, I'm sorry, okay.


00:16:19.040 --> 00:16:21.439
It's just a lot to deal with right now,
and I sort of want to be alone.


00:16:21.440 --> 00:16:22.679
Okay. I get it, yeah.


00:16:22.680 --> 00:16:23.839
And look, about the band...


00:16:23.840 --> 00:16:26.840
Don't even worry about the band, okay?
We'll use Phil's Song for Bandslam.


00:16:28.440 --> 00:16:31.119
Or not. We don't have to use Phil's Song.
We can find another song, or...


00:16:31.120 --> 00:16:34.120
Hey, go ahead. Knock yourselves out.


00:16:37.920 --> 00:16:40.920
I mean, it's a beautiful song, Charlotte.


00:16:41.160 --> 00:16:43.519
It would make your dad proud.
It would be like he's there.


00:16:43.520 --> 00:16:46.439
Stop! Please, just stop!


00:16:46.440 --> 00:16:48.319
There is no us, Will. I'm not in the band.


00:16:48.320 --> 00:16:51.320
What? No, no, no.
Okay, we'll find another song...


00:16:51.600 --> 00:16:54.439
It's not about the song. I quit. I just quit.


00:16:54.440 --> 00:16:55.839
-Why?
-I don't do "why"!


00:16:55.840 --> 00:16:58.840
No, you have to. You just have to!


00:17:05.520 --> 00:17:08.520
Please.


00:17:13.600 --> 00:17:15.999
You really want to know why?


00:17:16.000 --> 00:17:19.000
Last summer, when my dad got sick,


00:17:20.520 --> 00:17:23.520
I promised God, the universe,


00:17:25.680 --> 00:17:28.199
anyone who'd listen,


00:17:28.200 --> 00:17:30.399
that I'd be different.


00:17:30.400 --> 00:17:33.400
Better. Nicer.


00:17:34.840 --> 00:17:37.840
My dad hated the way I acted
when I was with Ben.


00:17:38.440 --> 00:17:41.440
The way I treated kids who weren't popular.


00:17:41.680 --> 00:17:44.319
So, I changed.


00:17:44.320 --> 00:17:47.320
I started volunteering with the monsters.
I left my friends. I left my band.


00:17:49.480 --> 00:17:52.480
I left everything that set me apart
from people like...


00:17:54.000 --> 00:17:57.000
Me.


00:17:58.800 --> 00:18:01.800
People like me.


00:18:03.280 --> 00:18:06.119
So we were just this


00:18:06.120 --> 00:18:08.959
experiment to try and make your dad okay?


00:18:08.960 --> 00:18:10.839
No, I know how crazy this must sound...


00:18:10.840 --> 00:18:13.799
Honestly, Charlotte,
the thing that never made sense


00:18:13.800 --> 00:18:16.800
was you being my friend in the first place.


00:18:19.720 --> 00:18:22.720
Hey!
While you're up there on your high horse,


00:18:23.000 --> 00:18:26.000
ask yourself who are you
to judge me about lying?


00:18:26.360 --> 00:18:29.360
Dewey!


00:18:34.160 --> 00:18:36.479
That stands for DWI, right?


00:18:36.480 --> 00:18:39.480
Driving while intoxicated?


00:18:40.560 --> 00:18:43.560
I don't know what's worse.


00:18:44.720 --> 00:18:47.720
Losing a father you love so much
you change your whole life for him,


00:18:53.080 --> 00:18:56.080
or having a father you're so ashamed of,
you make up a whole life for him.


00:19:32.160 --> 00:19:34.879
Can I have some beef jerky?


00:19:34.880 --> 00:19:37.880
Is he kidding?


00:19:39.640 --> 00:19:42.640
You warned me about her.


00:19:42.720 --> 00:19:44.439
I didn't listen.


00:19:44.440 --> 00:19:47.440
She can't help it.
It's how girls like that are hardwired.


00:19:50.520 --> 00:19:53.520
How are we hardwired?


00:19:53.720 --> 00:19:56.720
I mean, sure, right now, I am just a kid.


00:19:58.600 --> 00:20:01.600
Whatever.


00:20:02.560 --> 00:20:05.439
What's going to change?


00:20:05.440 --> 00:20:07.639
Nothing.


00:20:07.640 --> 00:20:10.239
I'm just going to be


00:20:10.240 --> 00:20:13.240
unhappy,


00:20:14.200 --> 00:20:15.999
alone,


00:20:16.000 --> 00:20:19.000
scared of, like, everything.


00:20:22.800 --> 00:20:25.800
You're not alone, Will.


00:20:33.120 --> 00:20:36.120
Experiment? We were just her experiment?


00:20:36.960 --> 00:20:38.839
I keep thinking...


00:20:38.840 --> 00:20:40.159
What?


00:20:40.160 --> 00:20:43.160
Well, if you were just part of
Charlotte's experiment this whole time,


00:20:44.320 --> 00:20:46.759
